<title>GERMANY: Wella says sees improved profits in 1997.</title>
<headline>Wella says sees improved profits in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>DARMSTADT 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>German haircare group Wella AG said on Tuesday that it expects its sales to rise 7.0 percent this year and it expects a clear improvement in profits.</p>
<p>The group reported its 1996 net profit climbed to 78.04 million marks ($45.8 million) from 74.15 million marks, while parent net profit rose to 60.6 million marks from 57.8 million marks.</p>
<p>Wella said that it saw its growth potential in the introduction of new products as well as the improvement of distribution channels and access to new markets and market segments. ($ = 1.703 German Marks)</p>
</text>
